Joining the NPTEL pinternship was a new experience for me because I had not worked with technologies like JavaScript, React, or MongoDB before. In the beginning, everything felt confusing and unfamiliar. I had to put in extra effort to understand how things worked, especially while going through the lessons and activities.

The learning process was not always easy. Some topics took time to understand, and there were moments when I felt slow compared to others. But instead of giving up, I decided to stay consistent and continue learning at my own pace. Slowly, things started becoming clearer, and I began to feel more confident with the concepts.

This pinternship helped me improve not only my technical knowledge but also my attitude toward learning. I learned how important patience and regular practice are. Even though the internship is still going on, I can already see a positive change in the way I approach new topics and challenges.

Overall, this experience has been helpful and meaningful, and it has encouraged me to keep learning and improving step by step.

